# SciVance Software License

## Acceptance

In order to get any license under these terms, you must agree to them as both strict obligations and conditions to all your licenses.

## Free Private Use

An individual may use the software without a seat and free of charge for private use.  **Private use** is study, hobby projects and personal research that the individual does for themselves.  It does not include any use by or for a business, any use in work for which anyone is paid, or any use by or for an organization of any kind, including a government institution, a charity, a school or university, or a public research, health or safety organization.  Private use needs no registration and no contact with the licensor.

## Seats

Any use that is not private use needs a seat.  Each seat covers one individual developer.

A seat is bought from the licensor.  To get one, contact the licensor through https://gabrielmoraru.com/about-me/.  A seat covers any purpose, commercial or noncommercial.

A seat covers the major version of the software it was bought for, including every later release of that major version (for example 3.0, 3.1 and 3.2), with no time limit.  It does not cover a later major version of the software (for example 4.0); that needs a new seat.

## Copyright License

The licensor grants you a copyright license for the software to do everything you might do with the software that would otherwise infringe the licensor's copyright in it for any purpose.  However, you may only distribute the software according to [Distribution](#distribution) and make changes or new works based on the software according to [Changes and New Works License](#changes-and-new-works-license).

## Distribution

**You may not give the software to anyone else.**  The only place from which anyone may get the software is the licensor's repository, https://github.com/GabrielOnDelphi/Autopilot-for-Delphi.  You have no license to distribute, publish, sell, lend, mirror, host, or otherwise make the software available to any other person, in any form: to share it, point people at that repository.  This covers the source code, the compiled unit files (`.dcu`), the executable files, packages, archives, copies of the repository, uploads to a package registry or file-sharing service, and inclusion in any library, component set, template, sample project, course material, or software development kit.  It covers a changed or derived version of the software exactly as it covers the original.

Everyone who gets the software gets it under these terms: without a seat, they may use it only for private use.

An application of your own into which the software is built is different: you may build and run it for your own use, but you may not give it to any other person, including customers, unless you hold a separate distribution license obtained from the licensor.  A seat does not include a distribution license.

Two narrow permissions for such an application, and nothing beyond them:

### 1. Your own application with the bridge inactive

You may give other people an application of your own that you built without the `AUTOPILOT` conditional define.  In such a build the bridge is inactive: it opens no connection and accepts no commands.  This permission does not cover any build made with the `AUTOPILOT` conditional define.  Conditions:

  a. You distribute the application in compiled form - an executable, an installer, a mobile application package, or similar.
  b. What you distribute does not contain the source code of the software, its `.dcu` files, or any other form from which a person could recover the software as a unit reusable in their own projects.
  c. Your own use of the software is covered by a seat or is private use.

You owe no credit, notice, or attribution inside your application for this permission.

### 2. Testing inside your company

This permission is an exception to the rule above that you may not give an application of your own into which the software is built to any other person.

You may give another individual in your company who holds a seat of their own, for testing only:

  a. a test application of your own that you built with the test client of the software (`Autopilot.Client.pas`), and
  b. a build of your own application that you made with the `AUTOPILOT` conditional define.

A build server or test machine that you control may build and run these applications under your seat.  Conditions:

  a. You give these applications in compiled form only.  What you give does not contain the source code of the software, its `.dcu` files, or any other form from which a person could recover the software as a unit reusable in their own projects.
  b. These applications are used only to test your own application.
  c. Your own use of the software is covered by a seat.

This permission does not cover giving these applications to anyone outside your company, or to anyone who does not hold a seat of their own.

